# Narrow build context for scripts/engramhalo/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile fetches its pinned source and the upstream packaging
# patches over git from inside the build (it does not COPY the source
# tree). The ONE exception is a single, explicitly reviewed local patch
# override file under patches/ (see that file's own header and the
# Dockerfile comments around UPSTREAM_QWEN38_PATCH_SHA256 /
# REVIEWED_QWEN38_OVERRIDE_SHA256 for why it exists and how it is
# hash-verified before use). This .dockerignore exists as defense in depth
# so an operator running `docker build` from this directory never
# accidentally sends real host/runtime state to the build daemon, even
# though a COPY now exists for that one reviewed patch file.
#
# Deny by default, everything not explicitly needed for the build:
*

# Allow only the files this recipe actually documents/uses as build inputs.
!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore
!README.md
!build-manifest.example.json
!config.example.json
!patches
!patches/llama-cpp-qwen38-per-buffer-mmap.rebased-for-15176583.patch

# Belt-and-suspenders: explicitly re-exclude anything that could carry
# private/local state or model weights even if a broader `!` rule above
# were loosened later.
.git
.git/
**/.git/
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.gguf
*.safetensors
models/
**/models/
state/
**/state/
runtime_state_dir/
**/runtime_state_dir/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
